IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sea-schooling`

-- School Education Act 1999 (WA), with the School Education Regulations 2000 (WA), ss 4-6, 9-11H, 23-30, 38-42, 75-79, 97-106; regs 11B-16, 61-64 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (the School Education Regulations 2000 are used as deposited).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_school-education-act-1999_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Dates of birth are those in the workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-{chloe,jake,daniel}/facts.json: Chloe
-- 14 March 2003, Jake 30 August 2006, Daniel 9 April 1996, Oliver 5 September 2030, Luca 2 February 2030. The event
-- dates are the events' own. Facts the lives do not state (visa, intake area, what the school has free, the content of
-- an absence) are HYPOTHETICAL and named as such in the fixtures.

§ `fixtures`

`enrolled at the local school` MEANS `My child's arrangements` WITH
    `enrolled at a school` IS TRUE
    `a parent is registered as home educator` IS FALSE
    `exempted by the Minister, conditions being complied with` IS FALSE
    `a section 11D notice is in force` IS FALSE
    `a section 11H notice of full-time employment is in force` IS FALSE
    `part-time employment with every section 11H(6) condition met` IS FALSE

`registered for home education` MEANS `My child's arrangements` WITH
    `enrolled at a school` IS FALSE
    `a parent is registered as home educator` IS TRUE
    `exempted by the Minister, conditions being complied with` IS FALSE
    `a section 11D notice is in force` IS FALSE
    `a section 11H notice of full-time employment is in force` IS FALSE
    `part-time employment with every section 11H(6) condition met` IS FALSE

`not enrolled anywhere` MEANS `My child's arrangements` WITH
    `enrolled at a school` IS FALSE
    `a parent is registered as home educator` IS FALSE
    `exempted by the Minister, conditions being complied with` IS FALSE
    `a section 11D notice is in force` IS FALSE
    `a section 11H notice of full-time employment is in force` IS FALSE
    `part-time employment with every section 11H(6) condition met` IS FALSE

`a TAFE course under a section 11D notice in force` MEANS `My child's arrangements` WITH
    `enrolled at a school` IS FALSE
    `a parent is registered as home educator` IS FALSE
    `exempted by the Minister, conditions being complied with` IS FALSE
    `a section 11D notice is in force` IS TRUE
    `a section 11H notice of full-time employment is in force` IS FALSE
    `part-time employment with every section 11H(6) condition met` IS FALSE

`an unexplained day away` MEANS `My child's absence` WITH
    `the school was open for instruction` IS TRUE
    `prevented by temporary physical or mental incapacity` IS FALSE
    `prevented by another reasonable cause` IS FALSE
    `I told the principal the cause as soon as practicable` IS FALSE
    `school days after the absence started before I told the principal` IS 10
    `the principal asked for a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I gave a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I have applied or intend to apply for home education, and told the principal in writing` IS FALSE
    `the principal required my child to stay away on public health grounds` IS FALSE
    `a recognised religious or cultural day, at a government school` IS FALSE
    `I told the principal beforehand, or as soon as reasonably practicable where beforehand was not` IS FALSE

`sick, school told the next day` MEANS `My child's absence` WITH
    `the school was open for instruction` IS TRUE
    `prevented by temporary physical or mental incapacity` IS TRUE
    `prevented by another reasonable cause` IS FALSE
    `I told the principal the cause as soon as practicable` IS TRUE
    `school days after the absence started before I told the principal` IS 1
    `the principal asked for a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I gave a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I have applied or intend to apply for home education, and told the principal in writing` IS FALSE
    `the principal required my child to stay away on public health grounds` IS FALSE
    `a recognised religious or cultural day, at a government school` IS FALSE
    `I told the principal beforehand, or as soon as reasonably practicable where beforehand was not` IS FALSE

`sick, school told after 5 school days` MEANS `My child's absence` WITH
    `the school was open for instruction` IS TRUE
    `prevented by temporary physical or mental incapacity` IS TRUE
    `prevented by another reasonable cause` IS FALSE
    `I told the principal the cause as soon as practicable` IS TRUE
    `school days after the absence started before I told the principal` IS 5
    `the principal asked for a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I gave a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I have applied or intend to apply for home education, and told the principal in writing` IS FALSE
    `the principal required my child to stay away on public health grounds` IS FALSE
    `a recognised religious or cultural day, at a government school` IS FALSE
    `I told the principal beforehand, or as soon as reasonably practicable where beforehand was not` IS FALSE

`a religious day, school not told` MEANS `My child's absence` WITH
    `the school was open for instruction` IS TRUE
    `prevented by temporary physical or mental incapacity` IS FALSE
    `prevented by another reasonable cause` IS FALSE
    `I told the principal the cause as soon as practicable` IS FALSE
    `school days after the absence started before I told the principal` IS 10
    `the principal asked for a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I gave a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I have applied or intend to apply for home education, and told the principal in writing` IS FALSE
    `the principal required my child to stay away on public health grounds` IS FALSE
    `a recognised religious or cultural day, at a government school` IS TRUE
    `I told the principal beforehand, or as soon as reasonably practicable where beforehand was not` IS FALSE

`a day away in the school holidays` MEANS `My child's absence` WITH
    `the school was open for instruction` IS FALSE
    `prevented by temporary physical or mental incapacity` IS FALSE
    `prevented by another reasonable cause` IS FALSE
    `I told the principal the cause as soon as practicable` IS FALSE
    `school days after the absence started before I told the principal` IS 10
    `the principal asked for a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I gave a medical certificate` IS FALSE
    `I have applied or intend to apply for home education, and told the principal in writing` IS FALSE
    `the principal required my child to stay away on public health grounds` IS FALSE
    `a recognised religious or cultural day, at a government school` IS FALSE
    `I told the principal beforehand, or as soon as reasonably practicable where beforehand was not` IS FALSE

`an Australian child living in Perth` MEANS `My child's residence` WITH
    `usually resides in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `entitled to reside permanently in Australia` IS TRUE
    `in the International Secondary Student Exchange Programme` IS FALSE
    `a dependant of a Schedule 1 scholarship holder` IS FALSE
    `covered by the Status of Forces Agreement` IS FALSE
    `the visa subclass held` IS 0
    `the visa subclass validly applied for, with the letter` IS 0

`a child in Perth on a subclass 482 visa` MEANS `My child's residence` WITH
    `usually resides in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `entitled to reside permanently in Australia` IS FALSE
    `in the International Secondary Student Exchange Programme` IS FALSE
    `a dependant of a Schedule 1 scholarship holder` IS FALSE
    `covered by the Status of Forces Agreement` IS FALSE
    `the visa subclass held` IS 482
    `the visa subclass validly applied for, with the letter` IS 0

`a child in Perth on a subclass 600 visitor visa` MEANS `My child's residence` WITH
    `usually resides in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `entitled to reside permanently in Australia` IS FALSE
    `in the International Secondary Student Exchange Programme` IS FALSE
    `a dependant of a Schedule 1 scholarship holder` IS FALSE
    `covered by the Status of Forces Agreement` IS FALSE
    `the visa subclass held` IS 600
    `the visa subclass validly applied for, with the letter` IS 0

`the local school, full` MEANS `The school's offer` WITH
    `we live in its intake area` IS TRUE
    `an appropriate educational programme is available` IS TRUE
    `classroom accommodation is available` IS FALSE

`a school outside our intake area, full` MEANS `The school's offer` WITH
    `we live in its intake area` IS FALSE
    `an appropriate educational programme is available` IS TRUE
    `classroom accommodation is available` IS FALSE

`a school with a programme and a free classroom` MEANS `The school's offer` WITH
    `we live in its intake area` IS FALSE
    `an appropriate educational programme is available` IS TRUE
    `classroom accommodation is available` IS TRUE

